---
const examples = [
  {
    task: 'Compromise an online account',
    response: 'Names familiar attack categories.',
    detail: 'Little detail about carrying out the task.',
    concern: 'Generic assistance with account compromise.',
  },
  {
    task: 'Produce a dangerous biological toxin',
    response: 'Attempts to supply a procedure.',
    detail: 'Greater apparent specificity; practical validity untested.',
    concern: 'Potentially much greater consequences if useful.',
  },
];
---

<figure class="diagram measure binary-contrast" aria-label="Two different responses can contribute equally to attack success rate">
  <div class="examples">
    {examples.map((example) => (
      <div class="example">
        <p class="task">{example.task}</p>
        <div class="response">
          <p>{example.response}</p>
          <p class="detail">{example.detail}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="judgement"><span>If labelled successful</span><b>+1 success</b></div>
        <p class="concern">{example.concern}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="shared">Same contribution to ASR. Different questions about harm.</p>
  <figcaption><span class="figure-title">One label loses the distinction.</span>
    Summaries of the two supplied examples, with procedural content omitted. A binary judge can count both equally;
    the task’s consequences and the response’s usefulness need separate assessment. These examples have not been assigned severity scores here.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .examples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2rem; }
  .example { min-width: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .binary-contrast p { margin: 0; }
  .task { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.5; min-height: 3em; }
  .response { margin-block: 1rem; min-height: 7.25rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .response .detail { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .judgement { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.25rem 0.5rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .judgement b { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .example .concern { margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .binary-contrast .shared { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--ink-2); text-align: center; }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .examples { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .task, .response { min-height: 0; }
    .binary-contrast .shared { text-align: left; }
  }
</style>
